## How the evaluation stays honest

- 20% stratified holdout locked before any label-based analysis, scored **once**; a lock file refuses any other pipeline or threshold.
- Repeated stratified 5-fold CV (3 repeats) on the other 80%; all preprocessing and resampling inside training folds; leakage guards in the test suite.
- Comparisons and decision rules written down before results ([pre-registration](notes/00_preregistration.md), with dated amendments): a more complex option replaces a simpler one only if the 95% CI of the paired difference (corrected resampled t-test) excludes 0.
- Every number in this README, the model card, notebook 00 and the project page is generated from committed artifacts in `reports/`.

## Run it

```bash
uv sync              # Python 3.12 environment from uv.lock
make check           # ruff + pytest (incl. leakage/split guards) + docs/website freshness + JS tests
make notebooks       # re-execute notebooks 00–06 in order; results land in reports/
make docs            # regenerate README.md, docs/model_card.md and web/site/ from reports/
make web-serve       # preview the project page at http://localhost:8000
make kaggle          # rebuild Kaggle editions
make content-preview # low-res previews of the 3-D content figures (full renders: Actions → Content figures)
```

The whole pipeline runs on a laptop in a few minutes (seed 42, deterministic).

## Scoring API

`api/` serves the same exported model as the website (`reports/p4_web_model.json`) with pure-Python scoring: `POST /predict` returns the fraud score, the decision at the project threshold (`approve` / `step-up`) and the three largest per-feature contributions (coefficient × model input, log-odds); `GET /health` reports the model id. Requests are validated with pydantic (types, ranges, known categories, no extra fields). Tests check that the API's score equals the Python pipeline's for all 2,000 transactions on the website (≤ 1e-9). The threshold comes from **illustrative assumed costs (not bank data)**.

```bash
# with uv (from the repo; model files are read from reports/)
uv sync
uv run uvicorn api.app:app --port 8000

# or with Docker (python:3.12-slim, non-root; built and smoke-tested in CI)
docker build -t fraud-console-api .
docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 fraud-console-api

# then, in another terminal (example_request.json is a real dev transaction)
curl -s localhost:8000/health
curl -s -X POST localhost:8000/predict -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @api/example_request.json
```

Interactive docs: <http://localhost:8000/docs>. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs lint, pytest, the Node tests, builds the image and calls `/predict` inside the container.

